## Context

During the AEDIST raid on 2026-06-11 (background job, tickets 0505-0507),
`/gaze 949` was invoked twice. Both times the skill returned immediately as
"completed (forked execution)" with a result like "Three reviewers launched
in parallel ... waiting for them to complete" — but the fork had already
exited. The reviewers were `run_in_background` agents; when the fork ends
its turn, nobody is left to receive their completion notifications, so they
evaporate: no verdict, no PR comment, nothing in the parent session's
TaskList. Interactive sessions don't hit this because the fork's loop stays
alive to await the children.

Workaround used (worked for PRs #949/#955/#960 of aedist-technical-report):
the caller launches the reviewer pair as awaited foreground Agent calls
(`model: sonnet`, read-only), fixes findings, then calls `/verify-gate`,
which completes synchronously and posts its verdict. Recorded in AEDIST
project memory as `feedback_gaze_fork_dies_in_background_jobs.md`.

## Relevant files

- `skills/gaze/SKILL.md` — the phase that launches the three reviewers
  (adherence, built-in review, multi-perspective panel)

## Actions

1. Make the reviewer launches blocking inside the fork: either issue the
   three Agent calls in one message as foreground (parallel, awaited) calls,
   or follow each background launch with an explicit await before the skill
   text allows the turn to end.
2. State the concurrency contract in the skill text (rules/workflow.md:
   every multi-item step declares parallel-background vs sequential-blocking
   and why) — here: parallel-foreground, because a forked skill must not end
   its turn with children in flight.

## Test

- In a background (non-interactive) session, run `/gaze <PR>` on a trivial
  open PR: the skill result must contain the reviewers' outputs (or the gate
  verdict), not a "waiting for them to complete" message.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `/gaze` never ends its forked turn while reviewer agents are in flight
- [ ] Skill text declares the launch mode per the concurrency-discipline rule
- [ ] Background-session run produces a posted verdict end-to-end
